# Line endings, decided 2026-09-02.
#
# THE CONVENTION IS LF, for every JSON file in the tree. Not a style
# preference — a correctness one, and it was `tools/resources/
# check_resources_1990.py` failing 2 of 60 that forced the choice.
#
# WHY IT BROKE. The 1990 provenance chain hashes file BYTES: the `meta.
# source_sha256` block of `spheres-sim/data/resources_1990.json` pins the
# sha256 of four inputs, and the checker re-hashes those four off disk. This
# repo is checked out with `core.autocrlf=true` and carried no `.gitattributes`
# at all, so every JSON blob (LF, as git stores it) lands in a Windows worktree
# as CRLF, and a digest is a digest OF ONE OF THOSE TWO FILES. The recorded
# block had drifted into holding both conventions at once — LF-blob hashes for
# district_population.json and districts.json, CRLF-worktree hashes for
# district_resources.json and transcribed_1990_six_lines.json — so on this
# machine exactly two of the four could pass and no re-pin of the other two
# could ever fix it. The same root cause failed CHECK 5's "the committed file
# uses LF newlines only" and its byte-for-byte regeneration bar.
#
# WHY LF AND NOT CRLF. Three reasons, in order of weight. The checker already
# had a bar demanding LF (`b"\r" not in committed`), so LF is the house
# convention already written down. Git already stores every one of these files
# with LF, so this rule changes no blob — only what a checkout writes. And a
# byte-hash of a transcribed data file is a claim about the DATA (iron rule 4);
# it must not depend on which OS checked it out, or the nightly Linux run and
# the Windows session will disagree forever about provenance that never moved.
#
# Scope is `*.json` because every JSON here is transcribed data or a generated
# artifact — 148 of them, the 137 nation records included — and the provenance
# rule should hold for all of them, not only the four that happened to be
# hashed today.
*.json text eol=lf
# The terrain generator also compares this generated Rust file byte for byte.
spheres-web/ui/terrain-tiles/embed.rs text eol=lf
# These source files are also byte-hashed by the leadership production inventory.
spheres-sim/src/nations.rs text eol=lf
spheres-sim/src/government.rs text eol=lf
# C01 also records exact bytes of its census/production readers.
tools/avatars/leadership_production.py text eol=lf
tools/avatars/person_art_pipeline.py text eol=lf
tools/avatars/fictional_art_pipeline.py text eol=lf
tools/avatars/campaign_census.py text eol=lf
tools/avatars/campaign_research.py text eol=lf
tools/avatars/import_cnccfp_census.py text eol=lf
# The official C01 discovery snapshot is hashed as downloaded, not normalized.
docs/campaign-certification/C01/research/sources/** -text -whitespace

